---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
const KEYS = Array.from({ length: 10 }, (_, i) => i + 1);
const ROWS = [['src', 'Source table'], ['dw', 'Dual-write'], ['pl', 'Polling'], ['cdc', 'Log-based CDC']];
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Four ways to copy a table" hint="The same 60 seconds of inserts, updates and deletes on a 10-row table are copied to a search index three ways. The connector crashes in the middle. Which copy still matches the source at the end?">
  <ol class="how">
    <li>At the defaults (log-based CDC, offsets committed every 10 changes, a blind sink), <b>dual-write ends with 3 wrong rows</b> and <b>polling leaves 3 deleted rows in the index for ever</b>. <b>CDC ends with 0 wrong rows</b>, but it replays 8 changes after the restart and the blind sink grows <b>1 duplicate row</b>. The source log also passes its 25-change cap during the outage.</li>
    <li>Tick <b>idempotent sink</b>: the same 8 replayed changes are ignored by comparing the log position, so there are no duplicates and no step backwards. Choose <b>commit after every change</b> and only 1 change is replayed.</li>
    <li>Choose <b>commit before processing</b>: nothing is replayed, but the change being handled at the crash is <b>lost</b> for good. Choose <b>never commit</b>: the whole log is replayed, and the source must keep all 59 changes, so its disk fills at second 25.</li>
    <li>Choose <b>commit after every change</b>, set the downtime to <b>40</b> and switch to <b>keep only the last N changes</b>: the source does not run out of disk, but the connector's position has been purged and it cannot resume without a new snapshot.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="pg cdb" data-cdb>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Connector crashes while handling change # <input type="range" min="1" max="55" value="18" data-crash /> <b data-crashval></b></label>
      <label>Down for (seconds, 0 = no crash) <input type="range" min="0" max="40" value="20" data-down /> <b data-downval></b></label>
      <label>Offsets are committed <select class="pg-in" data-policy>
        <option value="every">after every change is applied</option>
        <option value="batch" selected>after every 10 changes</option>
        <option value="before">before the change is applied</option>
        <option value="never">never</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>The sink <select class="pg-in" data-idem>
        <option value="blind" selected>applies every event it receives (blind)</option>
        <option value="idem">ignores a change older than the stored position</option>
      </select></label>
    </div>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <label>Poll every (seconds) <input type="range" min="1" max="10" value="5" data-poll /> <b data-pollval></b></label>
      <label>When the source log is too big <select class="pg-in" data-drop>
        <option value="slot" selected>keep it until the connector confirms (replication slot)</option>
        <option value="drop">keep only the last N changes</option>
      </select></label>
      <label>Log cap N (changes) <input type="range" min="10" max="60" value="25" data-cap /> <b data-capval></b></label>
    </div>
    <div class="tw" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Final value of each key by method"><table class="cmp">
      <caption class="sr">Value of each row key in the source and in each copy at the end. A dash means the row is absent.</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th>{KEYS.map((k) => <th scope="col">{k}</th>)}</tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {ROWS.map(([id, label]) => <tr><th scope="row">{label}</th>{KEYS.map(() => <td data-cell={id}></td>)}</tr>)}
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
    <div class="pg-grid">
      <div class="pg-box" data-b1><h3>Dual-write</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o1></span><span class="pg-note" data-n1></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b2><h3>Polling by updated_at</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o2></span><span class="pg-note" data-n2></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b3><h3>Log-based CDC</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o3></span><span class="pg-note" data-n3></span></div>
      <div class="pg-box" data-b4><h3>The source's retained log</h3><span class="pg-mono" data-o4></span><span class="pg-note" data-n4></span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="pg-out" data-verdict aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="pg-note">Model: one change per second for 60 seconds on rows 1 to 10, about 6% rolled back and about 20% of the others in a transaction that commits 4 seconds late (the log is in commit order). Dual-write writes the index right after the database, and 6% of those index writes fail with no retry; it is also lost while the index is cut off during the outage, and 20% of its writes arrive 3 seconds late. Polling runs a query for rows with updated_at after its cursor and cannot see deletes. The connector applies 2 changes per second. When the source keeps the log for the connector, the log is everything after the last committed offset; it refuses writes while that is over the cap. A row shown like 512 x2 is a duplicate.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<style>
  .tw { overflow-x: auto; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .cmp { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font: .82rem ui-monospace, monospace; min-width: 560px; }
  .cmp th, .cmp td { border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 4px 6px; text-align: center; }
  .cmp thead th { background: var(--surface-2); }
  .cmp tbody th { text-align: left; background: var(--surface-2); font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; }
  .cmp td.bad { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bad) 18%, var(--surface)); color: var(--bad-text); font-weight: 700; }
  .sr { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; clip-path: inset(50%); white-space: nowrap; }
</style>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-cdb]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = <T extends HTMLElement>(s: string) => root.querySelector<T>(s)!;
    const KEYS = 10; const TICKS = 60; const SVC = 0.5;
    type Op = { ts: number; key: number; kind: string; value: number | null; rollback: boolean; sinkFail: boolean; jit: boolean; slow: boolean; commit: number; lsn: number };
    const SEED = 77;
    const DELETE_RATE = 0.3; // share of writes to an existing key that delete it
    const VALUE = { min: 100, span: 900 }; // row values 100..999
    const ROLLBACK_RATE = 0.06, SINK_FAIL_RATE = 0.06; // transactions rolled back; dual writes that fail at the sink
    const JITTER = { rate: 0.2, delayS: 3 }, NET_S = 0.1; // dual writes delayed in the network, and the base network delay
    const SLOW = { rate: 0.2, window: 5, delayS: 4 }; // long transactions commit 4 s late (only when the next 5 ops leave the key alone)
    const BATCH = 10; // offsets committed every 10 events
    const SCAN = { endS: 120, stepS: 0.5 }; // backlog scan for the replication slot
    const POLL_END_S = 80;
    // linear congruential generator (Numerical Recipes constants)
    let seed = SEED; const rnd = () => ((seed = (seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) % 4294967296) / 4294967296);
    const state = new Map<number, number>(); const ops: Op[] = [];
    for (let ts = 0; ts < TICKS; ts++) {
      const key = 1 + Math.floor(rnd() * KEYS); const has = state.has(key);
      const kind = !has ? 'insert' : rnd() < DELETE_RATE ? 'delete' : 'update';
      const value = VALUE.min + Math.floor(rnd() * VALUE.span);
      const rollback = rnd() < ROLLBACK_RATE; const sinkFail = rnd() < SINK_FAIL_RATE; const jit = rnd() < JITTER.rate; const slowWant = rnd() < SLOW.rate;
      if (!rollback) { if (kind === 'delete') state.delete(key); else state.set(key, value); }
      ops.push({ ts, key, kind, value: kind === 'delete' ? null : value, rollback, sinkFail, jit, slow: slowWant, commit: ts, lsn: 0 });
    }
    ops.forEach((o, i) => { o.slow = o.slow && !o.rollback && !ops.slice(i + 1, i + 1 + SLOW.window).some((p) => p.key === o.key); o.commit = o.ts + (o.slow ? SLOW.delayS : 0); });
    const truth = state;
    const LOG = ops.filter((o) => !o.rollback).sort((a, b) => a.commit - b.commit || a.ts - b.ts).map((o, i) => ({ ...o, lsn: i + 1 }));
    const N = LOG.length;
    const compare = (m: Map<number, number>) => {
      let ghost = 0; let missing = 0; let stale = 0;
      for (let k = 1; k <= KEYS; k++) { const a = truth.get(k); const b = m.get(k); if (a === b) continue; if (a === undefined) ghost++; else if (b === undefined) missing++; else stale++; }
      return { ghost, missing, stale, wrong: ghost + missing + stale };
    };
    type P = { crash: number; down: number; policy: string; idem: boolean; poll: number; drop: boolean; cap: number };
    function cdc(p: P) {
      const X = Math.min(p.crash, N); const crashes = p.down > 0;
      const commitAfter = (j: number) => (p.policy === 'every' ? j : p.policy === 'batch' ? Math.floor(j / BATCH) * BATCH : p.policy === 'before' ? j : 0);
      const delivered: { lsn: number; t: number; replay: boolean }[] = []; const steps: [number, number][] = [[0, 0]];
      let prev = 0; let committed = 0; let tc = -1; let tr = -1; let purged = 0;
      const run = (j: number, t0: number, replay: boolean) => {
        const start = Math.max(LOG[j - 1].commit, t0); const done = start + SVC; prev = done;
        delivered.push({ lsn: j, t: done, replay }); committed = Math.max(committed, commitAfter(j));
        steps.push([p.policy === 'before' ? start : done, committed]);
      };
      for (let j = 1; j <= (crashes ? X - 1 : N); j++) run(j, prev, false);
      if (crashes) {
        tc = Math.max(LOG[X - 1].commit, prev); tr = tc + p.down;
        if (p.policy === 'before') { committed = Math.max(committed, X); steps.push([tc, committed]); } // committed, then the process died before applying
        else { delivered.push({ lsn: X, t: tc + SVC, replay: false }); } // applied, then died before committing
        const avail = LOG.filter((e) => e.commit <= tr).length;
        let r = committed + 1;
        if (p.drop && avail > p.cap && r < avail - p.cap + 1) { purged = avail - p.cap + 1 - r; r = avail - p.cap + 1; }
        prev = tr;
        for (let j = r; j <= N; j++) run(j, prev, j <= X && !(p.policy === 'before' && j === X));
      }
      const seen = new Set(delivered.map((d) => d.lsn)); const lost = LOG.filter((e) => !seen.has(e.lsn)).map((e) => e.lsn);
      const rows = new Map<number, number[]>(); const lsnOf = new Map<number, number>(); const maxLsn = new Map<number, number>(); let dupIgnored = 0; let backwards = 0;
      delivered.sort((a, b) => a.t - b.t);
      for (const d of delivered) {
        const e = LOG[d.lsn - 1];
        if (p.idem) {
          if (d.lsn <= (lsnOf.get(e.key) || 0)) { dupIgnored++; continue; }
          lsnOf.set(e.key, d.lsn); if (e.kind === 'delete') rows.delete(e.key); else rows.set(e.key, [e.value as number]);
        } else {
          if (d.lsn < (maxLsn.get(e.key) || 0)) backwards++;
          maxLsn.set(e.key, Math.max(maxLsn.get(e.key) || 0, d.lsn));
          if (e.kind === 'insert') { const r = rows.get(e.key) || []; r.push(e.value as number); rows.set(e.key, r); }
          else if (e.kind === 'update') { const r = rows.get(e.key); if (r) rows.set(e.key, r.map(() => e.value as number)); }
          else rows.delete(e.key);
        }
      }
      const view = new Map<number, number>(); let dupRows = 0; rows.forEach((r, k) => { view.set(k, r[r.length - 1]); dupRows += r.length - 1; });
      const lags = delivered.filter((d) => !d.replay).map((d) => d.t - LOG[d.lsn - 1].commit);
      const availAt = (t: number) => LOG.filter((e) => e.commit <= t).length; const commitAt = (t: number) => steps.reduce((m, s) => (s[0] <= t ? Math.max(m, s[1]) : m), 0);
      let peak = 0; let peakAt = 0; let fullAt = -1; const blocked = new Set<number>();
      for (let t = 0; t <= SCAN.endS; t += SCAN.stepS) { const r = availAt(t) - commitAt(t); if (r > peak) { peak = r; peakAt = t; } if (!p.drop && r > p.cap) { if (fullAt < 0) fullAt = t; if (t < TICKS) blocked.add(Math.floor(t)); } }
      const rejected = p.drop ? 0 : LOG.filter((e) => blocked.has(e.commit)).length;
      return { view, rows, ...compare(view), dupRows, dupDeliveries: delivered.filter((d) => d.replay).length, dupIgnored, backwards, lost, purged, tc, tr, peak, peakAt, fullAt, rejected, lagAvg: lags.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / lags.length, lagMax: Math.max(...lags) };
    }
    function dual(tc: number, tr: number) {
      const arr = ops.map((o) => ({ ...o, arr: o.ts + (o.jit ? JITTER.delayS : 0) + NET_S })).sort((a, b) => a.arr - b.arr || a.ts - b.ts);
      const m = new Map<number, number>(); const lastTs = new Map<number, number>(); let dropped = 0; let phantom = 0; let swapped = 0;
      for (const o of arr) {
        if (o.sinkFail || (tc >= 0 && o.ts >= tc && o.ts < tr)) { dropped++; continue; }
        if (o.rollback) phantom++;
        if (o.ts < (lastTs.get(o.key) ?? -1)) swapped++;
        lastTs.set(o.key, o.ts);
        if (o.kind === 'delete') m.delete(o.key); else m.set(o.key, o.value as number);
      }
      return { view: m, ...compare(m), dropped, phantom, swapped };
    }
    function poll(every: number, tc: number, tr: number) {
      const m = new Map<number, number>(); const db = new Map<number, { v: number; upd: number }>(); const got = new Set<string>(); const lags: number[] = [];
      let cursor = -1; let idx = 0;
      for (let t = 0; t <= POLL_END_S; t++) {
        while (idx < LOG.length && LOG[idx].commit <= t) { const e = LOG[idx++]; if (e.kind === 'delete') db.delete(e.key); else db.set(e.key, { v: e.value as number, upd: e.ts }); }
        if (t % every !== 0 || (tc >= 0 && t >= tc && t < tr)) continue;
        let mx = cursor;
        db.forEach((r, k) => { if (r.upd > cursor) { m.set(k, r.v); mx = Math.max(mx, r.upd); got.add(`${k}:${r.upd}`); lags.push(t - (LOG.find((e) => e.key === k && e.ts === r.upd)?.commit ?? t)); } });
        cursor = mx;
      }
      const late = LOG.filter((e) => e.slow && e.kind !== 'delete' && !got.has(`${e.key}:${e.ts}`)).length;
      return { view: m, ...compare(m), seenV: got.size, late, lagAvg: lags.length ? lags.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / lags.length : 0, lagMax: lags.length ? Math.max(...lags) : 0 };
    }
    const cells: Record<string, HTMLElement[]> = {};
    root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-cell]').forEach((c) => { (cells[c.dataset.cell as string] ||= []).push(c); });
    const f1 = (n: number) => n.toFixed(1);
    const plural = (n: number, w: string) => `${n} ${w}${n === 1 ? '' : 's'}`;
    function draw() {
      const crash = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-crash]').value); const down = Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-down]').value);
      const p: P = { crash, down, policy: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-policy]').value, idem: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-idem]').value === 'idem', poll: Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-poll]').value), drop: q<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-drop]').value === 'drop', cap: Number(q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-cap]').value) };
      q('[data-crashval]').textContent = String(Math.min(crash, N)); q('[data-downval]').textContent = String(down); q('[data-pollval]').textContent = String(p.poll); q('[data-capval]').textContent = String(p.cap);
      q<HTMLInputElement>('[data-crash]').disabled = down === 0;
      const c = cdc(p); const d = dual(c.tc, c.tr); const pl = poll(p.poll, c.tc, c.tr);
      const show = (id: string, get: (k: number) => string, ref: (k: number) => string) => cells[id].forEach((cell, i) => { const k = i + 1; const s = get(k); cell.textContent = s; cell.classList.toggle('bad', id !== 'src' && s !== ref(k)); });
      const val = (m: Map<number, number>) => (k: number) => (m.has(k) ? String(m.get(k)) : '—');
      const srcV = val(truth);
      show('src', srcV, srcV); show('dw', val(d.view), srcV); show('pl', val(pl.view), srcV);
      show('cdc', (k) => { const r = c.rows.get(k); return r ? String(r[r.length - 1]) + (r.length > 1 ? ` x${r.length}` : '') : '—'; }, srcV);
      const colour = (i: number, bad: boolean) => q<HTMLElement>(`[data-b${i}]`).style.setProperty('--c', bad ? 'var(--bad)' : 'var(--good)');
      q('[data-o1]').textContent = `${plural(d.wrong, 'wrong row')} of ${Math.max(truth.size, 1)} live`;
      q('[data-n1]').textContent = `${d.missing} missing, ${d.ghost} extra, ${d.stale} stale. ${plural(d.dropped, 'write')} lost (index failures${c.tc >= 0 ? ' and the outage' : ''}), ${plural(d.phantom, 'rolled-back write')} kept, ${plural(d.swapped, 'write')} applied out of order. No lag, but also nothing to replay from.`;
      colour(1, d.wrong > 0);
      q('[data-o2]').textContent = `${plural(pl.wrong, 'wrong row')}`;
      q('[data-n2]').textContent = `${pl.ghost} deleted rows still in the index (a deleted row has no updated_at to find). Saw ${pl.seenV} of ${N} row versions. ${plural(pl.late, 'late commit')} stepped over by the cursor. Lag ${f1(pl.lagAvg)} s on average, ${f1(pl.lagMax)} s at worst.`;
      colour(2, pl.wrong > 0);
      q('[data-o3]').textContent = `${plural(c.wrong, 'wrong row')}${c.dupRows > 0 ? `, ${plural(c.dupRows, 'duplicate row')}` : ''}`;
      q('[data-n3]').textContent = (down === 0 ? 'No crash. ' : `${plural(c.dupDeliveries, 'change')} delivered twice${p.idem ? `, ${c.dupIgnored} ignored by the sink` : `, ${c.backwards} write${c.backwards === 1 ? '' : 's'} that moved a row back to an older value for a moment`}. `)
        + (c.lost.length > 0 ? `${plural(c.lost.length, 'change')} never delivered (#${c.lost.slice(0, 4).join(', #')}${c.lost.length > 4 ? '...' : ''}). ` : '') + `Lag ${f1(c.lagAvg)} s on average, ${f1(c.lagMax)} s at worst.`;
      colour(3, c.wrong > 0 || c.dupRows > 0 || c.lost.length > 0);
      const slotFull = !p.drop && c.fullAt >= 0; const gone = p.drop && c.purged > 0;
      q('[data-o4]').textContent = `peak ${c.peak} changes kept (cap ${p.cap})`;
      q('[data-n4]').textContent = slotFull ? `Over the cap from second ${Math.round(c.fullAt)}: the source would refuse ${plural(c.rejected, 'write')} because its disk is full.`
        : gone ? `${plural(c.purged, 'change')} the connector still needed were purged. It cannot resume and needs a new snapshot.` : p.drop ? 'Within the cap. The connector could resume from its offset.' : 'Within the cap.';
      colour(4, slotFull || gone);
      const out = q('[data-verdict]');
      const bad = d.wrong > 0 || pl.wrong > 0 || c.wrong > 0 || c.lost.length > 0 || c.dupRows > 0 || slotFull || gone;
      out.classList.toggle('bad', bad);
      const parts: string[] = [];
      parts.push(`Dual-write ${d.wrong} wrong, polling ${pl.wrong} wrong, log-based CDC ${c.wrong} wrong.`);
      if (pl.ghost > 0) parts.push(`Polling cannot see deletes: ${plural(pl.ghost, 'row')} stay in the index for ever.`);
      if (down > 0 && p.policy === 'before') parts.push(`Committing before applying never repeats a change, but the one in flight (#${c.lost[0] ?? X(crash)}) is lost${c.wrong === 0 ? ' (here a later change happened to overwrite it)' : ''}.`);
      else if (down > 0 && p.policy === 'never') parts.push(`With no committed offset every restart replays from the start (${plural(c.dupDeliveries, 'change')}), and the source has to keep the whole log.`);
      else if (down > 0 && c.dupDeliveries > 0) parts.push(p.idem ? 'The idempotent sink absorbed every replayed change, so at-least-once delivery is safe.' : (c.dupRows > 0 || c.backwards > 0 ? 'The blind sink was not safe against replays: it grew duplicate rows or moved rows back in time. Make the sink idempotent.' : 'The replayed changes happened to be updates and deletes, so the blind sink survived by luck.'));
      if (slotFull) parts.push(`A connector that is down holds the log: the source reached its cap at second ${Math.round(c.fullAt)}.`);
      if (gone) parts.push('Limiting the log protects the source, and costs you a full re-snapshot of the table.');
      out.textContent = parts.join(' ');
    }
    const X = (n: number) => Math.min(n, N);
    root.addEventListener('input', draw); root.addEventListener('change', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
